Experiment 15 (env-knob bundle) - NOT FOR COMMIT. The A/B rig that found the cheapest
form of the CP_BLIT (r2d) write-visibility fix on A7XX (docs/bugs-found.md Bug 1,
analysis.md 21.10-21.11). TU_B2I_SYNC selects what the driver does after every
vkCmdCopyBufferToImage; TU_B2I_COUNT counts copies and copies-per-command-buffer.

  0  off: 19 MISMATCH - the b2i -> i2b chain in one submit reads pre-copy memory
  1  FD_CCU_CLEAN_COLOR + WFI after every copy      (the validated reference, 94/94)
  2  FD_CCU_CLEAN_BLIT_CACHE + WFI                  FAIL - the blit/resolve cache
  3  FD_CCU_CLEAN_BLIT_CACHE alone                  FAIL   is not what r2d writes go through
  4  CLEAN_COLOR + CACHE_INVALIDATE + WFI           PASS
  5  BLIT_CACHE + CACHE_INVALIDATE + WFI            FAIL
  6  CLEAN_COLOR + CACHE_INVALIDATE, no WFI         PASS
  9/12/14 = 1/4/6 deferred (flush once per group of copies in the next blit setup): PASS
  7  lazy bits: flush_bits |= CCU_CLEAN_COLOR|WAIT_FOR_IDLE, nothing executed here -
     the next natural flush point pays: PASS 94/94, stable over repeats
  15 the lazy bits without the WFI: PASS (kept only as a control, the WFI is proven
     necessary in the per-copy form, see analysis.md 21.10)

Verdict: mode 7 is the shipping form, see patches/0013-turnip-b2i-ccu-clean.patch.
